{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794405917000-engineer-cc3-fix-r8.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md; git diff -- test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc test/yin/repl/query_test.cljc test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc'","aggregated_output":"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-11 14:19:17 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-11 21:19:17 +07\n\n# cc3 fix round r8 — failed retention observable (F1) + targeted regression (F4)\n\nWorktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3`, branch `cc3-lowering-provenance`, HEAD `0ec036d1` + uncommitted r7 fix. Nothing committed.\n\nDeliverable mirror: the requested path under `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/` is outside this session's writable roots, so this file is the mirror at `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/collab/yang-clojure/1794405917000-engineer-cc3-fix-r8.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md` (per the prompt's \"or mirror + say so\").\n\n## F1 (P1) — failed retention is now observable, program execution preserved\n\n**Red first.** `/tmp/cc3-r8-red.clj`: a store refusing only provenance writes (payload-keyed on `:yin.vm.provenance/schema` / `:yin.repl.call-provenance/schema`) produced `t3=\"42\"`, `handles=nil`, `observable? false` for both relation and record writes — the r7 blanket catch swallowed the only signal. After the fix the same probe prints `42\\nWarning: this round's call provenance was not retained (relation write failed: store refused the provenance write); the program's value is unaffected` (resp. `record write failed: …`), `observable? true`.\n\n**Fix** (`src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc`), r7's failure isolation kept, silence removed:\n\n- `retain-packet-call-provenance!` now tags every throw with its stage via `retention-throw`: `:validation` (provenance validation refusal), `:relation` (relation `materialize!`), `:record` (record `materialize!`), plus admission and root. Its throwing contract is otherwise unchanged.\n- `run-evaluator-stage`'s `retaining-load` records, for a **claimed** admission only, `{:admission :root :stage :message}` into a failures volatile. No handle is assoc'd for a failed packet; completed handles in the same round still merge as before. An unclaimed packet (no entry in `:call-site-round-claims`) or a nil retention (no store / no claim) records nothing — failed retention is distinguished from an unclaimed admission.\n- Failures ride the session state as `:call-provenance-failures` (public accessor `yin.repl/call-provenance-failures`) beside `:call-provenance-handles`, and the round's slice as `:call-provenance-round-failures`, which `with-index-notice` renders as a second Warning line (`retention-notice`: `Warning: this round's call provenance was not retained (relation write failed: <msg>); the program's value is unaffected`) and consumes. This is the observable surface that works when indexing succeeded and the indexer (`index.cljc:549`, indexer state only, running before retention) has nothing to report. The Warning text is additive only — existing index/query contracts (`3\\nWarning: … materialize failed …`) still pass unmodified; no test contract was changed.\n- Replay/recovery semantics unchanged and extended to failures the same way as handles (r3/r4 pattern): evaluator-stage throws carry `::call-provenance-failures`/`::call-provenance-round-failures` on the ex-info, `link-raise` carries them, `run-evaluation`'s catch and `recheck-pending*` merge them into the recovered session (`retention-recovery-failures` prefers a carried cumulative value, else appends the round increment). Successful-path retention (F3-confirmed) is untouched.\n\n## F4 (P2) — targeted regression: indexing succeeds, provenance persistence fails\n\nNew durable tests, each covering **both** the relation write and the record write with a payload-keyed selective store:\n\n- `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc` `repl-retention-failure-is-observable-test`: healthy defs first (handles present), then the store starts refusing only provenance writes; `(g)` still answers `42`, the Warning names the failed stage, exactly one admission-scoped failure with the right `:stage` is recorded, handles equal the earlier set (no incomplete handle, earlier survive), and an unclaimed literal round adds no failure and no Warning.\n- `test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc` `a-retention-only-failure-is-reported-though-indexing-succeeds`: `(+ 1 2)` warns with the retention diagnostic while `repl-state` shows `:published? true` and `:failure nil`.\n- `test/yin/repl/query_test.cljc` `a-retention-only-failure-still-answers-queries`: `dao.space.query/q` still answers (no `index-unavailable`), the retention Warning is present, no handle, failures recorded.\n\nExisting durable/recovery tests kept and green alongside.\n\n## Verification\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| RED probe `/tmp/cc3-r8-red.clj` (before fix) | `observable? false` both stages |\n| Same probe after fix | Warning + diagnostic both stages, value `42` preserved |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test -n yin.repl.index-test -n yin.repl.query-test` | 84 tests / 1038 assertions, **0 failures** |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yin.repl.index-test -n yin.repl.query-test -n yin.repl-test -n yin.repl.store-test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test` | 163 tests / 1438 assertions, **0 failures** |\n| `clj -M:kondo --lint src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc test/yin/repl/query_test.cljc` | **0 errors, 0 warnings** |\n| Full `clojure -M:test` | timed out at 300 s in this session — **unverified**, not claimed green |\n\nNote: one intermediate assertion (repeat `(g)` is unclaimed) failed on first run — each round mints a fresh admission, so a repeat call *is* claimed; the test now uses an unclaimed literal round instead. Contract change stated above: none to existing tests; the only new surface is the additive Warning line, `call-provenance-failures`, and `:call-provenance-failures` on session state.\n\nDiff: `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc` + 3 test files (includes the pre-existing uncommitted r7 change to repl.cljc). Commit: none, as instructed.\ndiff --git a/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc b/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc\nindex 66b07374..fd78b0c1 100644\n--- a/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc\n+++ b/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc\n@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@\n             [clojure.string :as str]\n             [clojure.walk :as walk]\n             [dao.jing :as jing]\n+            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n             [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n             [dao.space.index :as space.index]\n             [dao.space.query :as query]\n@@ -2195,3 +2196,51 @@\n                    \"retrieval after reopening the store answers the same relation\")\n                (yin.repl.store/close! reopened))))\n          (finally (cleanup))))))\n+\n+\n+(deftest repl-retention-failure-is-observable-test\n+  ;; cc3 r8 F1+F4: indexing succeeds but provenance persistence fails\n+  ;; (relation write, then record write): evaluation completes, the\n+  ;; failure is observable as the round's Warning and as an\n+  ;; admission-scoped session diagnostic, no incomplete handle is\n+  ;; advertised, and earlier completed handles survive.\n+  (doseq [[label fail-key stage]\n+          [[\"relation write\" :yin.vm.provenance/schema :relation]\n+           [\"record write\" :yin.repl.call-provenance/schema :record]]]\n+    (testing label\n+      (let [fail? (atom false)\n+            inner (mem/create-content-mem)\n+            store (assoc inner\n+                         :put-bytes-fn\n+                         (fn [address bs]\n+                           (let [v (try (cbor/decode bs)\n+                                        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception\n+                                                  :cljs :default) _ nil))]\n+                             (when (and @fail? (map? v)\n+                                        (contains? v fail-key))\n+                               (throw (ex-info \"store refused the provenance write\"\n+                                               {})))\n+                             ((:put-bytes-fn inner) address bs))))\n+            [s1 _] (repl/eval-input\n+                     (repl-frontends/create-state {:index-store store})\n+                     \"(def k (fn [] 1))\")\n+            [s2 _] (repl/eval-input s1 \"(def g (fn [] (+ (k) 41)))\")\n+            handles-before (repl/call-provenance-handles s2)]\n+        (is (seq handles-before) \"precondition: earlier retention completed\")\n+        (reset! fail? true)\n+        (let [[s3 text] (repl/eval-input s2 \"(g)\")\n+              failures (repl/call-provenance-failures s3)]\n+          (is (str/starts-with? text \"42\\nWarning: \")\n+              \"evaluation completes; the failure rides the round's Warning\")\n+          (is (str/includes? text \"call provenance was not retained\"))\n+          (is (str/includes? text (str label \" failed\")))\n+          (is (= 1 (count failures)))\n+          (is (= stage (:stage (first failures))))\n+          (is (some? (:admission (first failures)))\n+              \"the diagnostic is admission-scoped\")\n+          (is (= handles-before (repl/call-provenance-handles s3))\n+              \"no incomplete handle; earlier completed handles survive\")\n+          (let [[s4 text4] (repl/eval-input s3 \"42\")]\n+            (is (= \"42\" text4)\n+                \"an unclaimed round records no failure and warns not\")\n+            (is (= failures (repl/call-provenance-failures s4)))))))))\ndiff --git a/test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc b/test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc\nindex bcecf41f..7106da3c 100644\n--- a/test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc\n+++ b/test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc\n@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@\n             [clojure.string :as str]\n             [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n             [dao.jing :as jing]\n+            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n             [dao.jing.file :as jing.file]\n             [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n             [dao.space.index :as index]\n@@ -550,6 +551,39 @@\n         \"the manifest and every node blob are read back from the store\")))\n \n \n+(deftest a-retention-only-failure-is-reported-though-indexing-succeeds\n+  ;; cc3 r8 F1/F4: the store refuses only provenance writes, so the\n+  ;; indexer publishes and has nothing to report; the round must still\n+  ;; warn — through the retention diagnostic, not the indexer.\n+  (doseq [[label fail-key]\n+          [[\"relation write\" :yin.vm.provenance/schema]\n+           [\"record write\" :yin.repl.call-provenance/schema]]]\n+    (testing label\n+      (let [inner (mem/create-content-mem)\n+            store (assoc inner\n+                         :put-bytes-fn\n+                         (fn [address bs]\n+                           (let [v (try (cbor/decode bs)\n+                                        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception\n+                                                  :cljs :default) _ nil))]\n+                             (when (and (map? v) (contains? v fail-key))\n+                               (throw (ex-info \"store refused the provenance write\"\n+                                               {})))\n+                             ((:put-bytes-fn inner) address bs))))\n+            [state [text]] (evaluate\n+                             (repl.frontends/create-state {:index-store store})\n+                             [\"(+ 1 2)\"])\n+            status (get-in (repl/repl-state state) [:index])]\n+        (is (str/starts-with? text \"3\\nWarning: \"))\n+        (is (str/includes? text \"call provenance was not retained\"))\n+        (is (str/includes? text (str label \" failed\")))\n+        (is (true? (:published? status)) \"indexing itself succeeded\")\n+        (is (nil? (:failure status)) \"the indexer has no failure to report\")\n+        (is (empty? (repl/call-provenance-handles state))\n+            \"no handle is advertised for the failed retention\")\n+        (is (= 1 (count (repl/call-provenance-failures state))))))))\n+\n+\n (deftest a-publication-failure-is-reported-in-the-round-and-repl-state\n   (let [broken {:put-bytes-fn (fn [_address _bytes]\n                                 (throw (ex-info \"store refused the write\" {})))\ndiff --git a/test/yin/repl/query_test.cljc b/test/yin/repl/query_test.cljc\nindex b458a599..02629a7d 100644\n--- a/test/yin/repl/query_test.cljc\n+++ b/test/yin/repl/query_test.cljc\n@@ -6,6 +6,8 @@\n    non-evaluating reader, so quoted forms are spelled `(quote ...)`.\"\n   (:require [dao.test-slow :as slow] [clojure.string :as str]\n             [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n+            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n+            [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n             [dao.stream :as stream]\n             [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n             [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\n@@ -417,6 +419,35 @@\n                          \"could not be read\")))))\n \n \n+(deftest a-retention-only-failure-still-answers-queries\n+  ;; cc3 r8 F1/F4: indexing succeeds and queries answer, but provenance\n+  ;; persistence fails; the failure stays observable and no handle is\n+  ;; advertised for it.\n+  (doseq [[label fail-key]\n+          [[\"relation write\" :yin.vm.provenance/schema]\n+           [\"record write\" :yin.repl.call-provenance/schema]]]\n+    (testing label\n+      (let [inner (mem/create-content-mem)\n+            store (assoc inner\n+                         :put-bytes-fn\n+                         (fn [address bs]\n+                           (let [v (try (cbor/decode bs)\n+                                        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception\n+                                                  :cljs :default) _ nil))]\n+                             (when (and (map? v) (contains? v fail-key))\n+                               (throw (ex-info \"store refused the provenance write\"\n+                                               {})))\n+                             ((:put-bytes-fn inner) address bs))))\n+            [state [_required answered]]\n+            (evaluate (repl.frontends/create-state {:index-store store})\n+                      [require-line (q-line names-query)])]\n+        (is (not (str/includes? answered \"index-unavailable\"))\n+            \"the published index still answers\")\n+        (is (str/includes? answered \"call provenance was not retained\"))\n+        (is (empty? (repl/call-provenance-handles state)))\n+        (is (seq (repl/call-provenance-failures state)))))))\n+\n+\n (deftest an-empty-session-is-an-empty-database\n   (let [indexer (:indexer (repl.frontends/create-state))\n         response (query/answer indexer\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
