7\t(deftest a-publication-failure-is-reported-in-the-round-and-repl-state\n  1405\t\n  1406\t(defn- with-index-notice\n  1407\t  \"Append what the round's index steps lost, if anything, to its result\n  1408\t   text, one line per notice in the order given; the evaluation's own\n  1409\t   answer is unchanged. A retention failure the evaluator stage\n  1410\t   recorded for this round (`:call-provenance-round-failures`, r8 F1)\n  1411\t   rides as a further Warning line and is consumed here, so a failed\n  1412\t   retention is observable in the round even when indexing succeeded\n  1413\t   and the indexer has nothing to report.\"\n  1414\t  [[state text] notices]\n  1415\t  (let [retention (retention-notice (:call-provenance-round-failures state))\n  1416\t        state (dissoc state :call-provenance-round-failures)\n  1417\t        notices (cond-> (vec (remove nil? notices))\n  1418\t                  retention (conj retention))]\n  1419\t    (if-let [notice (some->> notices seq (str/join \"\\n\"))]\n  1420\t      [state (if (str/blank? text) notice (str text \"\\n\" notice))]\n  1421\t      [state text])))\n  1422\t\n  1423\t\n  1424\t(defn call-site-tables\n  1425\t  \"The C1 side tables the session's expander retains, keyed by\n  1426\t   `[admission-origin final-root]` (`yin.vm.macro/call-site-table`\n M src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\n M test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc\n M test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc\n M test/yin/repl/query_test.cljc\n?? CC3-REVIEW-R7.md\n?? CC3-REVIEW-R8.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794357169000-engineer-cc3-lowering-provenance.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794374077000-engineer-cc3-fix-r2.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794376197000-engineer-cc3-fix-r3.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-cc3-f6-measure.clj\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-engineer-cc3-fix-r4.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794390804000-cc3-bounded-run-declaration-v2.md\n?? col